<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aichi Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aichi Prefecture is a prefecture in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagoya">Nagoya</a>. It was formed in 1871–1872 from the old provinces of Owari and Mikawa, the homelands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-nobunaga">Oda Nobunaga</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a>. Today it is one of Japan's main industrial regions and the home of the Toyota motor company.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aichi-prefecture.jpg" alt="Aichi Prefecture" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomio344456 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Westward_from_Sky_Deck_MIRAI360,_Nishiki_Naka_Ward_Nagoya_2022.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
